# .public-deny.example — template for params/.public-deny
#
# Copy to params/.public-deny (that folder is gitignored, so the file — and the
# identifiers in it — are never committed or synced to the public mirror).
#
# scripts/sync-to-public.sh reads params/.public-deny as a FAIL-CLOSED content
# deny-scan: one ERE regex per line ('#' = comment). If ANY pattern matches ANY
# file in the sanitized export tree, the sync ABORTS and nothing is published.
# This is defense-in-depth on top of the structural strips (terraform/, ansible/,
# envs/, params/, private-apps/, overlays/*/prod, users.yaml, *.tfvars/key/pem).
#
# IMPORTANT: CI publishes via .github/workflows/sync-to-public.yml, which
# materializes this list from the `PUBLIC_DENY_LIST` repo secret — NOT from this
# file. Keep the secret and this file in sync, or CI's scan will differ from a
# local `sync-to-public.sh` run.
#
# Add every private identifier that could leak through a non-stripped path:
your-real-domain\.com
your-github-owner
# Real usernames / handles (word-boundaried to avoid over-matching):
# \byourhandle\b
# Real RFC1918 ranges used in-cluster (also baked into platform.yaml / base manifests):
# \b10\.10\.[0-9]+\.[0-9]+\b
# \b10\.25\.[0-9]+\.[0-9]+\b
# Real storage/export paths:
# /mnt/YourPool/
